cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use open-rknpu in academic work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "open-rknpu"
abstract: >-
  An open, from-scratch compiler and runtime for the Rockchip RV1103 / RV1106 NPU
  with no vendor SDK, no RKNN library and no captured binaries. open-rknpu turns a
  static ONNX convolution graph into a task program the RV1103 NPU executes
  directly: an MIT-licensed Python compiler emits the register commands,
  weight/quantization blocks and container format itself, and a libc-only C runtime
  talks to /dev/rknpu and nothing else. Every claim in the repository is backed by a
  board run on the attached Luckfox Pico Mini B (rockchip,rv1106-rknpu, driver
  v0.8.2) and by integer-exact comparisons against an independent Python reference.
type: software
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-11"
repository-code: "https://github.com/open-rknpu/open-rknpu"
url: "https://github.com/open-rknpu/open-rknpu"
keywords:
  - rockchip
  - rv1103
  - rv1106
  - npu
  - onnx
  - compiler
  - edge-ai
  - reverse-engineering
